menu "ESP TFLite-Micro"

    config ESP_TFLITE_MICRO_USE_ESP_NN
        bool "Use ESP-NN optimized kernels"
        default y
        help
            When enabled (default), -DESP_NN is defined and the conv2d,
            depthwise-conv, fully-connected, mul, add, pooling and softmax kernels
            use the esp-nn component (SIMD/vector-optimized per target).

            When disabled, -DESP_NN is not defined. The esp_nn/ kernel wrappers are
            still compiled, but their optimized paths compile out and they fall back
            to TFLite Micro's own portable reference implementations. No application
            or example code needs to change (the per-kernel profiling symbols still
            exist). Useful for portability checks, debugging, and A/B benchmarking
            of esp-nn against the reference kernels.

endmenu
